<title>UK: ICO coffee exports rise in October.</title>
<headline>ICO coffee exports rise in October.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Coffee Organization (ICO) exporting members' exports rose to 6.03 million 60-kg bags in October from 4.84 million in September and 5.22 million in October 1995, ICO figures showed on Wednesday.</p>
<p>In the year from November 1995 to October 1996 total exports were 73.80 million bags from 65.29 million bags in the year ago period.</p>
<p>Latest ICO export data, in thousand bags, included -</p>
<p>		Oct 96    Oct 95    Nov95/Oct96   Nov94/Oct95</p>
<p>TOTAL	 6,028     5,216	73,803	  65,289</p>
<p>Brazil	2,149     1,172	13,545	  15,459</p>
<p>Colombia    1,016     1,043	10,738	   9,415</p>
<p>Guatemala     139	 121	 3,707	   3,611</p>
<p>Mexico	  163	 102	 4,644	   3,299</p>
<p>Indonesia     377	 484	 5,821	   3,363</p>
<p>Ivory Coast   104	 141	 2,703	   2,326</p>
<p>Uganda	  340	 173	 4,371	   2,804</p>
<p>Vietnam	 161	 233	 3,583	   3,349</p>
<p>Costa Rica    134	 163	 2,449	   1,927</p>
<p>El Salvador   184	  97	 2,335	   1,706</p>
<p>India	   154	 196	 3,155	   2,153</p>
<p>Peru	    174	 215	 1,455	   1,231</p>
<p>-- Clelia Oziel, London Newsroom +44-171-542 8072</p>
</text>
